/-!
# Complex line integrals and Abel-Jacobi vectors

Places, their residue fields, evaluation at rational places, divisors and the curve hypothesis
`IsCurveOver` come from the curve layer in `MathlibExt/AlgebraicGeometry/Curve/`. This file adds a
uniformizer and its coordinate differential at a place, the coefficient and the order of a
differential with respect to the coordinate differential, and, for a complex function field whose
places carry a topology and an atlas, the readings of functions and differentials in the preferred
charts, line integrals along paths and Abel-Jacobi vectors.

Every place of a curve over an algebraically closed field is rational, so a chart reads a function
through its values at places. Readings use the preferred chart `chartAt ℂ v` at each place `v`,
and these charts are required to be holomorphic coordinates (`IsHolomorphicAtlas`): in the
preferred chart at a place, every function regular there reads as a holomorphic function near the
centre of the chart, and the uniformizer reads as a local coordinate. The other charts of the atlas
are not constrained, and nothing here uses them.
A differential is read through its coefficient with respect to the coordinate differential, which
requires that differential to span (`Place.DCoordGenerates`).

A primitive of a differential along a path is a function of time that is, near each time, a local
primitive of the reading of the differential composed with the chart and the path. The line
integral along a path is the increment of a primitive, so it is defined for differentials with a
primitive along the path. It does not depend on the primitive, it is additive under concatenation
of paths and it changes sign under reversal. The Abel-Jacobi vector of a family of differentials
along a path collects these integrals. Modulo the period subgroup, generated by the integrals over
loops, it depends only on the endpoints of the path, and so does the Abel-Jacobi map on divisors
built from a choice of paths from a base place. For a basis of the regular differentials of a
compact curve, the period subgroup is the period lattice, and these maps lift the Abel-Jacobi map.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicCurve.Place.uniformizer` and `AlgebraicCurve.Place.dCoord`: an element of order one at
  a place and its Kähler differential.
* `AlgebraicCurve.Place.differentialCoeff` and `AlgebraicCurve.Place.ordDifferential`: the
  coefficient of a differential with respect to `dCoord`, and its order.
* `AlgebraicCurve.Place.chartRead` and `AlgebraicCurve.Place.readDifferential`: readings in the
  chart at a place.
* `AlgebraicCurve.IsHolomorphicAtlas`: the preferred charts are holomorphic coordinates.
* `AlgebraicCurve.IsPrimitiveAlong` and `AlgebraicCurve.pathIntegral`: primitives along a path and
  the line integral.
* `AlgebraicCurve.abelJacobiVec`, `AlgebraicCurve.abelJacobiDiv` and
  `AlgebraicCurve.periodSubgroup`: Abel-Jacobi vectors along paths, the Abel-Jacobi map on
  divisors and the period subgroup.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicCurve.IsPrimitiveAlong.pathIntegral_eq`: the line integral is the increment of every
  primitive.
* `AlgebraicCurve.pathIntegral_trans` and `AlgebraicCurve.pathIntegral_symm`: additivity under
  concatenation and change of sign under reversal.
* `AlgebraicCurve.pathIntegral_eq_sub_of_chartAt_eq`: along a path in one preferred chart, the line
  integral is the increment of a local primitive of the reading.
* `AlgebraicCurve.abelJacobiVec_sub_mem_periodSubgroup` and
  `AlgebraicCurve.abelJacobiDiv_sub_mem_periodSubgroup`: independence of the paths modulo periods.

## Implementation notes

The source reads differentials through a second choice of an element of order one, defines the
integral along every path with the value `0` when there is no primitive, and defines the
Abel-Jacobi vector of a pair of places through a chosen path, with the value `0` when there is
none. Here the reading uses the uniformizer, the integral takes a proof that a primitive exists,
and the Abel-Jacobi vector and map take their paths as arguments.
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

open IsLocalRing KaehlerDifferential
open scoped Manifold Topology

namespace AlgebraicCurve

variable (K F : Type*) [Field K] [Field F] [Algebra K F]

namespace Place

variable {K F}

variable (v : Place K F)

/-! ### Uniformizers and differentials -/

/-- **Uniformizer at a place.** An irreducible element of the valuation ring of `v`, chosen once
and for all and viewed in `F`. It has order one at `v`. -/
def uniformizer : F :=
  ((IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible v.toValuationSubring).choose : F)

theorem ord_uniformizer : v.ord v.uniformizer = 1 := by
  have hirr := (IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible v.toValuationSubring).choose_spec
  simpa [uniformizer] using v.ord_coe_irreducible hirr

theorem uniformizer_ne_zero : v.uniformizer ≠ 0 := by
  intro h
  simpa [h, v.ord_zero] using v.ord_uniformizer

/-- **Coordinate differential.** The Kähler differential of the uniformizer at `v`. -/
def dCoord : Ω[F⁄K] := KaehlerDifferential.D K F v.uniformizer

/-- **The coordinate differential spans.** The coordinate differential at `v` spans the Kähler
differentials of `F` over `K`, so every differential is a multiple of it. -/
class DCoordGenerates : Prop where
  span_eq_top : Submodule.span F {v.dCoord} = ⊤

theorem dCoord_ne_zero [v.DCoordGenerates] [Nontrivial Ω[F⁄K]] : v.dCoord ≠ 0 := by
  intro h0
  have htop := DCoordGenerates.span_eq_top (v := v)
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := exists_ne (0 : Ω[F⁄K])
  have hx_mem : x ∈ Submodule.span F {v.dCoord} := htop ▸ Submodule.mem_top
  rw [h0, Submodule.span_zero_singleton] at hx_mem
  exact hx hx_mem

theorem exists_eq_smul_dCoord [v.DCoordGenerates] (ω : Ω[F⁄K]) :
    ∃ f : F, ω = f • v.dCoord := by
  have hω : ω ∈ (⊤ : Submodule F Ω[F⁄K]) := Submodule.mem_top
  rw [← DCoordGenerates.span_eq_top (v := v), Submodule.mem_span_singleton] at hω
  exact hω.imp fun _ hf => hf.symm

/-- **Coefficient of a differential.** An element `f` of `F` with `ω = f • v.dCoord`. It is
defined only when `v.dCoord` spans the differentials, so that such an element exists, and it is
unique when the differentials are nontrivial. -/
def differentialCoeff [v.DCoordGenerates] (ω : Ω[F⁄K]) : F :=
  (v.exists_eq_smul_dCoord ω).choose

theorem differentialCoeff_smul_dCoord [v.DCoordGenerates] (ω : Ω[F⁄K]) :
    v.differentialCoeff ω • v.dCoord = ω :=
  (v.exists_eq_smul_dCoord ω).choose_spec.symm

theorem differentialCoeff_unique [v.DCoordGenerates] [Nontrivial Ω[F⁄K]]
    {ω : Ω[F⁄K]} {f : F} (hf : ω = f • v.dCoord) : v.differentialCoeff ω = f := by
  have key : (v.differentialCoeff ω - f) • v.dCoord = 0 := by
    rw [sub_smul, v.differentialCoeff_smul_dCoord ω, hf, sub_self]
  rcases smul_eq_zero.mp key with h | h
  · exact sub_eq_zero.mp h
  · exact absurd h v.dCoord_ne_zero

@[simp]
theorem differentialCoeff_dCoord [v.DCoordGenerates] [Nontrivial Ω[F⁄K]] :
    v.differentialCoeff v.dCoord = 1 :=
  v.differentialCoeff_unique (one_smul F v.dCoord).symm

@[simp]
theorem differentialCoeff_zero [v.DCoordGenerates] [Nontrivial Ω[F⁄K]] :
    v.differentialCoeff (0 : Ω[F⁄K]) = 0 :=
  v.differentialCoeff_unique (zero_smul F v.dCoord).symm

theorem differentialCoeff_smul [v.DCoordGenerates] [Nontrivial Ω[F⁄K]]
    (c : F) (ω : Ω[F⁄K]) :
    v.differentialCoeff (c • ω) = c * v.differentialCoeff ω :=
  v.differentialCoeff_unique
    (by rw [mul_smul, v.differentialCoeff_smul_dCoord])

/-- **Order of a differential at a place.** The order at `v` of the coefficient of `ω` with
respect to the coordinate differential at `v`. Since `Place.ord 0 = 0`, the zero differential has
order `0` when the differentials are nontrivial (`ordDifferential_zero`), not an infinite order of
vanishing. -/
def ordDifferential [v.DCoordGenerates] (ω : Ω[F⁄K]) : ℤ := v.ord (v.differentialCoeff ω)

@[simp]
theorem ordDifferential_zero [v.DCoordGenerates] [Nontrivial Ω[F⁄K]] :
    v.ordDifferential (0 : Ω[F⁄K]) = 0 := by
  rw [ordDifferential, v.differentialCoeff_zero, v.ord_zero]

theorem ordDifferential_dCoord [v.DCoordGenerates] [Nontrivial Ω[F⁄K]] :
    v.ordDifferential v.dCoord = 0 := by
  rw [ordDifferential, v.differentialCoeff_dCoord, v.ord_one]

theorem ordDifferential_smul [v.DCoordGenerates] [Nontrivial Ω[F⁄K]]
    {c : F} (hc : c ≠ 0) {ω : Ω[F⁄K]} (hω : v.differentialCoeff ω ≠ 0) :
    v.ordDifferential (c • ω) = v.ord c + v.ordDifferential ω := by
  rw [ordDifferential, ordDifferential, v.differentialCoeff_smul, v.ord_mul hc hω]

/-! ### Evaluation at rational places -/

/-- **Rational places.** Every place of a curve over an algebraically closed field is rational. -/
theorem isRational_of_isCurveOver [IsAlgClosed K] [IsCurveOver K F] : v.IsRational :=
  have := IsCurveOver.finiteResidueField v
  v.surjective_algebraMap_residueField_of_isAlgClosed

@[simp]
theorem evalAt_zero (hv : v.IsRational) : v.evalAt hv (0 : F) = 0 := by
  rw [v.evalAt_of_mem hv (zero_mem _)]
  have h0 : (⟨(0 : F), zero_mem _⟩ : v.toValuationSubring) = 0 := rfl
  rw [h0, map_zero, ← map_zero (algebraMap K v.ResidueField), v.residueInv_algebraMap hv]

/-! ### Readings in charts -/

variable {F : Type*} [Field F] [Algebra ℂ F]
variable [TopologicalSpace (Place ℂ F)] [ChartedSpace ℂ (Place ℂ F)] [IsCurveOver ℂ F]

/-- **Reading of a function in a chart.** At a point `z` of the target of the preferred chart at
`v`, the value of `f` at the place with coordinate `z`. Every place of a complex curve is rational,
so this is the complex number with the same residue as `f` at that place, and `0` at a pole of
`f`. -/
def chartRead (v : Place ℂ F) (f : F) : ℂ → ℂ :=
  fun z => ((extChartAt 𝓘(ℂ, ℂ) v).symm z).evalAt (isRational_of_isCurveOver _) f

theorem chartRead_apply (v : Place ℂ F) (f : F) (z : ℂ) :
    v.chartRead f z =
      ((extChartAt 𝓘(ℂ, ℂ) v).symm z).evalAt (isRational_of_isCurveOver _) f := rfl

@[simp]
theorem chartRead_zero (v : Place ℂ F) : v.chartRead 0 = 0 := by
  funext z
  simp [chartRead_apply]

end Place

variable {F : Type*} [Field F] [Algebra ℂ F]
variable [TopologicalSpace (Place ℂ F)] [ChartedSpace ℂ (Place ℂ F)] [IsCurveOver ℂ F]

variable (F) in
/-- **Holomorphic preferred charts.** The preferred charts `chartAt ℂ v` on the places of `F`,
which the readings use, are holomorphic coordinates: in the preferred chart at each place `v`,
every function regular at `v` reads as a function that is complex differentiable near the centre
of the chart, and the uniformizer at `v` reads with nonzero derivative at the centre, so it is a
holomorphic local coordinate at `v`. The other charts of the atlas are not constrained. -/
class IsHolomorphicAtlas : Prop where
  eventually_differentiableAt_chartRead (v : Place ℂ F) {f : F}
    (hf : f ∈ v.toValuationSubring) :
    ∀ᶠ z in 𝓝 (extChartAt 𝓘(ℂ, ℂ) v v), DifferentiableAt ℂ (v.chartRead f) z
  deriv_chartRead_uniformizer_ne_zero (v : Place ℂ F) :
    deriv (v.chartRead v.uniformizer) (extChartAt 𝓘(ℂ, ℂ) v v) ≠ 0

namespace Place

/-- **Readings of regular functions are analytic.** When the preferred charts are holomorphic
coordinates, the reading of a function regular at `v` in the preferred chart at `v` is analytic at
the centre of the chart. -/
theorem analyticAt_chartRead [IsHolomorphicAtlas F] (v : Place ℂ F) {f : F}
    (hf : f ∈ v.toValuationSubring) :
    AnalyticAt ℂ (v.chartRead f) (extChartAt 𝓘(ℂ, ℂ) v v) :=
  Complex.analyticAt_iff_eventually_differentiableAt.mpr
    (IsHolomorphicAtlas.eventually_differentiableAt_chartRead v hf)

/-- **Reading of a differential in a chart.** The reading of `ω` in the preferred chart at `v`, as
a multiple of `dz`: the reading of the coefficient of `ω` with respect to `v.dCoord`, times the
derivative of the reading of the uniformizer at `v`. -/
@[nolint unusedArguments] -- The class makes `deriv` the derivative of holomorphic maps.
def readDifferential [IsHolomorphicAtlas F] (v : Place ℂ F) [v.DCoordGenerates]
    (ω : Ω[F⁄ℂ]) : ℂ → ℂ :=
  fun z => v.chartRead (v.differentialCoeff ω) z * deriv (v.chartRead v.uniformizer) z

theorem readDifferential_apply [IsHolomorphicAtlas F] (v : Place ℂ F) [v.DCoordGenerates]
    (ω : Ω[F⁄ℂ]) (z : ℂ) :
    v.readDifferential ω z =
      v.chartRead (v.differentialCoeff ω) z * deriv (v.chartRead v.uniformizer) z := rfl

/-- **Reading of a multiple of the coordinate differential.** The differential `f • v.dCoord`
is read through its coefficient `f`. -/
theorem readDifferential_smul_dCoord [IsHolomorphicAtlas F] (v : Place ℂ F) [v.DCoordGenerates]
    (f : F) :
    v.readDifferential (f • v.dCoord) =
      fun z => v.chartRead f z * deriv (v.chartRead v.uniformizer) z := by
  funext z
  rw [readDifferential_apply, v.differentialCoeff_unique rfl]

@[simp]
theorem readDifferential_zero [IsHolomorphicAtlas F] (v : Place ℂ F) [v.DCoordGenerates] :
    v.readDifferential 0 = 0 := by
  funext z
  simp [readDifferential_apply]

end Place

section Integral

variable [IsHolomorphicAtlas F] [∀ v : Place ℂ F, v.DCoordGenerates]

/-! ### Primitives and line integrals -/

/-- **Primitive along a path.** `g` is a primitive of `ω` along the path `γ`: near each time `t₀`,
`g` agrees with the composite of `γ`, the preferred chart at `γ t₀` and a local primitive, in that
chart, of the reading of `ω` at `γ t₀`. -/
def IsPrimitiveAlong (ω : Ω[F⁄ℂ]) {P Q : Place ℂ F} (γ : Path P Q) (g : unitInterval → ℂ) :
    Prop :=
  ∀ t₀ : unitInterval, ∃ Φ : ℂ → ℂ,
    (∀ᶠ z in 𝓝 (extChartAt 𝓘(ℂ, ℂ) (γ t₀) (γ t₀)),
        HasDerivAt Φ ((γ t₀).readDifferential ω z) z) ∧
      ∀ᶠ t in 𝓝 t₀, g t = Φ (extChartAt 𝓘(ℂ, ℂ) (γ t₀) (γ t))

-- Two functions with the same derivative near a point differ by a constant near it.
private theorem eventually_sub_eq_of_hasDerivAt {f Φ₁ Φ₂ : ℂ → ℂ} {x₀ : ℂ}
    (h₁ : ∀ᶠ z in 𝓝 x₀, HasDerivAt Φ₁ (f z) z) (h₂ : ∀ᶠ z in 𝓝 x₀, HasDerivAt Φ₂ (f z) z) :
    ∀ᶠ z in 𝓝 x₀, Φ₁ z - Φ₂ z = Φ₁ x₀ - Φ₂ x₀ := by
  obtain ⟨ε, hε, hball⟩ := Metric.eventually_nhds_iff_ball.mp (h₁.and h₂)
  have hd : ∀ z ∈ Metric.ball x₀ ε, HasDerivAt (fun w => Φ₁ w - Φ₂ w) 0 z := fun z hz => by
    have h := (hball z hz).1.sub (hball z hz).2
    rw [sub_self] at h
    exact h
  filter_upwards [Metric.ball_mem_nhds x₀ hε] with z hz
  exact Metric.isOpen_ball.is_const_of_deriv_eq_zero (convex_ball x₀ ε).isPreconnected
    (fun w hw => (hd w hw).differentiableAt.differentiableWithinAt)
    (fun w hw => (hd w hw).deriv) hz (Metric.mem_ball_self hε)

-- Transport a local-primitive condition along an equality of places.
private theorem eventually_hasDerivAt_of_eq {ω : Ω[F⁄ℂ]} {Φ : ℂ → ℂ} {v w : Place ℂ F}
    (hvw : v = w)
    (h : ∀ᶠ z in 𝓝 (extChartAt 𝓘(ℂ, ℂ) v v), HasDerivAt Φ (v.readDifferential ω z) z) :
    ∀ᶠ z in 𝓝 (extChartAt 𝓘(ℂ, ℂ) w w), HasDerivAt Φ (w.readDifferential ω z) z := by
  subst hvw
  exact h

/-- **Primitive of the zero differential.** The zero function is a primitive of the zero
differential along every path. -/
theorem isPrimitiveAlong_zero {P Q : Place ℂ F} (γ : Path P Q) :
    IsPrimitiveAlong (0 : Ω[F⁄ℂ]) γ 0 := fun _ =>
  ⟨0, Filter.Eventually.of_forall fun z => by simp,
    Filter.Eventually.of_forall fun _ => rfl⟩

namespace IsPrimitiveAlong

variable {ω : Ω[F⁄ℂ]} {P Q R : Place ℂ F} {γ : Path P Q} {g g₁ g₂ : unitInterval → ℂ}

-- Near each time, two primitives along the same path differ by a constant.
private theorem eventually_sub_eq (h₁ : IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ g₁) (h₂ : IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ g₂)
    (t₀ : unitInterval) : ∀ᶠ t in 𝓝 t₀, g₁ t - g₂ t = g₁ t₀ - g₂ t₀ := by
  obtain ⟨Φ₁, hΦ₁, hg₁⟩ := h₁ t₀
  obtain ⟨Φ₂, hΦ₂, hg₂⟩ := h₂ t₀
  have hnear := ((continuousAt_extChartAt (γ t₀)).comp γ.continuous.continuousAt).eventually
    (eventually_sub_eq_of_hasDerivAt hΦ₁ hΦ₂)
  filter_upwards [hg₁, hg₂, hnear] with t ht₁ ht₂ ht
  rw [ht₁, ht₂, hg₁.self_of_nhds, hg₂.self_of_nhds]
  exact ht

/-- **Primitives have the same increment.** Two primitives of a differential along the same path
have the same increment. -/
theorem sub_eq_sub (h₁ : IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ g₁) (h₂ : IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ g₂) :
    g₁ 1 - g₁ 0 = g₂ 1 - g₂ 0 := by
  have h : g₁ 1 - g₂ 1 = g₁ 0 - g₂ 0 :=
    ((IsLocallyConstant.iff_eventually_eq _).mpr
      (h₁.eventually_sub_eq h₂)).apply_eq_of_preconnectedSpace 1 0
  linear_combination h

/-- **Primitive along the reversed path.** A primitive along `γ`, composed with the reversal of the
unit interval, is a primitive along the reversed path. -/
theorem symm (hg : IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ g) :
    IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ.symm (g ∘ unitInterval.symm) := fun t₀ => by
  obtain ⟨Φ, hΦ, hgΦ⟩ := hg (unitInterval.symm t₀)
  exact ⟨Φ, hΦ, (unitInterval.continuous_symm.tendsto t₀).eventually hgΦ⟩

/-- **Primitive along a concatenation.** Primitives along two composable paths glue to a primitive
along their concatenation, whose increment is the sum of their increments. -/
theorem exists_trans {γ' : Path Q R} {g' : unitInterval → ℂ} (hg : IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ g)
    (hg' : IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ' g') :
    ∃ k, IsPrimitiveAlong ω (γ.trans γ') k ∧ k 1 - k 0 = (g 1 - g 0) + (g' 1 - g' 0) := by
  let τ₁ : unitInterval → unitInterval := fun t => Set.projIcc 0 1 zero_le_one (2 * (t : ℝ))
  let τ₂ : unitInterval → unitInterval :=
    fun t => Set.projIcc 0 1 zero_le_one (2 * (t : ℝ) - 1)
  have hτ₁ : Continuous τ₁ :=
    continuous_projIcc.comp (continuous_const.mul continuous_subtype_val)
  have hτ₂ : Continuous τ₂ :=
    continuous_projIcc.comp ((continuous_const.mul continuous_subtype_val).sub continuous_const)
  let k : unitInterval → ℂ := fun t =>
    if (t : ℝ) ≤ 1 / 2 then g (τ₁ t) else g' (τ₂ t) + (g 1 - g' 0)
  have hk₁ : ∀ t : unitInterval, (t : ℝ) ≤ 1 / 2 → k t = g (τ₁ t) := fun t ht => ite_eq_left ht
  have hk₂ : ∀ t : unitInterval, ¬(t : ℝ) ≤ 1 / 2 → k t = g' (τ₂ t) + (g 1 - g' 0) :=
    fun t ht => ite_eq_right ht
  have hγ₁ : ∀ t : unitInterval, (t : ℝ) ≤ 1 / 2 → (γ.trans γ') t = γ (τ₁ t) := fun t ht => by
    change (if (t : ℝ) ≤ 1 / 2 then γ.extend (2 * t) else γ'.extend (2 * t - 1)) = _
    rw [ite_eq_left ht]
    rfl
  have hγ₂ : ∀ t : unitInterval, ¬(t : ℝ) ≤ 1 / 2 → (γ.trans γ') t = γ' (τ₂ t) :=
    fun t ht => by
      change (if (t : ℝ) ≤ 1 / 2 then γ.extend (2 * t) else γ'.extend (2 * t - 1)) = _
      rw [ite_eq_right ht]
      rfl
  refine ⟨k, fun t₀ => ?_, ?_⟩
  · rcases lt_trichotomy (t₀ : ℝ) (1 / 2) with hlt | heq | hgt
    · obtain ⟨Φ, hΦ, hgΦ⟩ := hg (τ₁ t₀)
      refine ⟨Φ, eventually_hasDerivAt_of_eq (hγ₁ t₀ hlt.le).symm hΦ, ?_⟩
      filter_upwards [(continuous_subtype_val.tendsto t₀).eventually (eventually_lt_nhds hlt),
        (hτ₁.tendsto t₀).eventually hgΦ] with t ht ht'
      rw [hk₁ t ht.le, hγ₁ t ht.le, hγ₁ t₀ hlt.le]
      exact ht'
    · have hτ₁₀ : τ₁ t₀ = 1 := Subtype.ext (by norm_num [τ₁, heq])
      have hτ₂₀ : τ₂ t₀ = 0 := Subtype.ext (by norm_num [τ₂, heq])
      obtain ⟨Φ₁, hΦ₁, hg₁⟩ := hg 1
      obtain ⟨Φ₂, hΦ₂, hg₂⟩ := hg' 0
      replace hΦ₁ := eventually_hasDerivAt_of_eq γ.target hΦ₁
      replace hΦ₂ := eventually_hasDerivAt_of_eq γ'.source hΦ₂
      rw [γ.target] at hg₁
      rw [γ'.source] at hg₂
      have hv₁ : g 1 = Φ₁ (extChartAt 𝓘(ℂ, ℂ) Q Q) := by
        have := hg₁.self_of_nhds
        rwa [γ.target] at this
      have hv₂ : g' 0 = Φ₂ (extChartAt 𝓘(ℂ, ℂ) Q Q) := by
        have := hg₂.self_of_nhds
        rwa [γ'.source] at this
      have ht₁ : Filter.Tendsto τ₁ (𝓝 t₀) (𝓝 1) := by
        have := hτ₁.tendsto t₀
        rwa [hτ₁₀] at this
      have ht₂ : Filter.Tendsto τ₂ (𝓝 t₀) (𝓝 0) := by
        have := hτ₂.tendsto t₀
        rwa [hτ₂₀] at this
      have ht₃ : Filter.Tendsto (fun t => extChartAt 𝓘(ℂ, ℂ) Q (γ' (τ₂ t))) (𝓝 t₀)
          (𝓝 (extChartAt 𝓘(ℂ, ℂ) Q Q)) := by
        have hγ' : Filter.Tendsto (fun t => γ' (τ₂ t)) (𝓝 t₀) (𝓝 Q) := by
          have := (γ'.continuous.tendsto 0).comp ht₂
          rwa [γ'.source] at this
        exact (continuousAt_extChartAt Q).tendsto.comp hγ'
      have hQ : (γ.trans γ') t₀ = Q := by rw [hγ₁ t₀ heq.le, hτ₁₀, γ.target]
      refine ⟨Φ₁, eventually_hasDerivAt_of_eq hQ.symm hΦ₁, ?_⟩
      rw [hQ]
      filter_upwards [ht₁.eventually hg₁, ht₂.eventually hg₂,
        ht₃.eventually (eventually_sub_eq_of_hasDerivAt hΦ₁ hΦ₂)] with t e₁ e₂ e₃
      by_cases ht : (t : ℝ) ≤ 1 / 2
      · rw [hk₁ t ht, hγ₁ t ht]
        exact e₁
      · rw [hk₂ t ht, hγ₂ t ht, e₂, hv₁, hv₂]
        linear_combination -e₃
    · obtain ⟨Φ, hΦ, hgΦ⟩ := hg' (τ₂ t₀)
      have hgt' : ¬(t₀ : ℝ) ≤ 1 / 2 := not_le.mpr hgt
      refine ⟨fun z => Φ z + (g 1 - g' 0), ?_, ?_⟩
      · refine eventually_hasDerivAt_of_eq (hγ₂ t₀ hgt').symm ?_
        filter_upwards [hΦ] with z hz using hz.add_const _
      · filter_upwards [(continuous_subtype_val.tendsto t₀).eventually (eventually_gt_nhds hgt),
          (hτ₂.tendsto t₀).eventually hgΦ] with t ht ht'
        rw [hk₂ t (not_le.mpr ht), hγ₂ t (not_le.mpr ht), hγ₂ t₀ hgt', ht']
  · have h0 : k 0 = g 0 := by
      rw [hk₁ 0 (by norm_num)]
      exact congrArg g (Subtype.ext (by norm_num [τ₁]))
    have h1 : k 1 = g' 1 + (g 1 - g' 0) := by
      rw [hk₂ 1 (by norm_num)]
      exact congrArg (· + (g 1 - g' 0)) (congrArg g' (Subtype.ext (by norm_num [τ₂])))
    rw [h0, h1]
    ring

end IsPrimitiveAlong

/-- **Primitives exist along the reversed path.** A differential with a primitive along `γ` has
one along the reversed path. -/
theorem exists_isPrimitiveAlong_symm {ω : Ω[F⁄ℂ]} {P Q : Place ℂ F} {γ : Path P Q}
    (h : ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ g) : ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ.symm g :=
  ⟨_, h.choose_spec.symm⟩

/-- **Primitives exist along a concatenation.** A differential with primitives along two composable
paths has one along their concatenation. -/
theorem exists_isPrimitiveAlong_trans {ω : Ω[F⁄ℂ]} {P Q R : Place ℂ F} {γ : Path P Q}
    {γ' : Path Q R} (h : ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ g) (h' : ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ' g) :
    ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong ω (γ.trans γ') g :=
  let ⟨k, hk, _⟩ := h.choose_spec.exists_trans h'.choose_spec
  ⟨k, hk⟩

/-- **Line integral along a path.** For a differential `ω` with a primitive along the path `γ`, the
increment `g 1 - g 0` of a primitive `g`. It does not depend on the primitive, and since the
preferred charts are holomorphic coordinates, it is the complex line integral of `ω` over `γ`. -/
def pathIntegral (ω : Ω[F⁄ℂ]) {P Q : Place ℂ F} (γ : Path P Q)
    (h : ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ g) : ℂ :=
  h.choose 1 - h.choose 0

/-- **Line integral as an increment.** The line integral along a path is the increment of every
primitive along it. -/
theorem IsPrimitiveAlong.pathIntegral_eq {ω : Ω[F⁄ℂ]} {P Q : Place ℂ F} {γ : Path P Q}
    {g : unitInterval → ℂ} (hg : IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ g) (h : ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ g) :
    pathIntegral ω γ h = g 1 - g 0 :=
  h.choose_spec.sub_eq_sub hg

theorem pathIntegral_zero {P Q : Place ℂ F} (γ : Path P Q)
    (h : ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong (0 : Ω[F⁄ℂ]) γ g) : pathIntegral 0 γ h = 0 := by
  rw [(isPrimitiveAlong_zero γ).pathIntegral_eq h, Pi.zero_apply, Pi.zero_apply, sub_zero]

theorem pathIntegral_refl (ω : Ω[F⁄ℂ]) (P : Place ℂ F)
    (h : ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong ω (Path.refl P) g) : pathIntegral ω (Path.refl P) h = 0 := by
  rw [pathIntegral, sub_eq_zero]
  refine ((IsLocallyConstant.iff_eventually_eq _).mpr fun t₀ => ?_).apply_eq_of_preconnectedSpace
    1 0
  obtain ⟨Φ, -, hgΦ⟩ := h.choose_spec t₀
  filter_upwards [hgΦ] with t ht
  rw [ht, hgΦ.self_of_nhds, Path.refl_apply, Path.refl_apply]

/-- **Line integral along the reversed path.** Reversing a path changes the sign of the line
integral. -/
theorem pathIntegral_symm {ω : Ω[F⁄ℂ]} {P Q : Place ℂ F} {γ : Path P Q}
    (h : ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ g) (h' : ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ.symm g) :
    pathIntegral ω γ.symm h' = -pathIntegral ω γ h := by
  rw [h.choose_spec.symm.pathIntegral_eq h', h.choose_spec.pathIntegral_eq h, Function.comp_apply,
    Function.comp_apply, unitInterval.symm_one, unitInterval.symm_zero, neg_sub]

/-- **Line integral along a concatenation.** The line integral along the concatenation of two
paths is the sum of the line integrals. -/
theorem pathIntegral_trans {ω : Ω[F⁄ℂ]} {P Q R : Place ℂ F} {γ : Path P Q} {γ' : Path Q R}
    (h : ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ g) (h' : ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ' g)
    (h'' : ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong ω (γ.trans γ') g) :
    pathIntegral ω (γ.trans γ') h'' = pathIntegral ω γ h + pathIntegral ω γ' h' := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk, hinc⟩ := h.choose_spec.exists_trans h'.choose_spec
  rw [hk.pathIntegral_eq h'', h.choose_spec.pathIntegral_eq h,
    h'.choose_spec.pathIntegral_eq h', hinc]

/-- **Primitive in one chart.** If the preferred chart at every point of `γ` is the chart `e`, and
near the image in `e` of each point of `γ` the reading of `ω` is the derivative of `Φ`, then
`Φ ∘ e ∘ γ` is a primitive of `ω` along `γ`. -/
theorem isPrimitiveAlong_of_chartAt_eq {ω : Ω[F⁄ℂ]} {P Q : Place ℂ F} {γ : Path P Q}
    {e : OpenPartialHomeomorph (Place ℂ F) ℂ} (he : ∀ t, chartAt ℂ (γ t) = e) {Φ : ℂ → ℂ}
    (hΦ : ∀ t, ∀ᶠ z in 𝓝 (e (γ t)), HasDerivAt Φ ((γ t).readDifferential ω z) z) :
    IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ fun t => Φ (e (γ t)) := fun t₀ => by
  have hx : ∀ y, extChartAt 𝓘(ℂ, ℂ) (γ t₀) y = e y := fun y => by
    rw [← he t₀]
    rfl
  refine ⟨Φ, ?_, Filter.Eventually.of_forall fun t => by rw [hx]⟩
  rw [hx]
  exact hΦ t₀

/-- **Line integral in one chart.** If the preferred chart at every point of `γ` is the chart `e`,
and near the image in `e` of each point of `γ` the reading of `ω` is the derivative of `Φ`, then
the line integral of `ω` along `γ` is `Φ (e Q) - Φ (e P)`. -/
theorem pathIntegral_eq_sub_of_chartAt_eq {ω : Ω[F⁄ℂ]} {P Q : Place ℂ F} {γ : Path P Q}
    {e : OpenPartialHomeomorph (Place ℂ F) ℂ} (he : ∀ t, chartAt ℂ (γ t) = e) {Φ : ℂ → ℂ}
    (hΦ : ∀ t, ∀ᶠ z in 𝓝 (e (γ t)), HasDerivAt Φ ((γ t).readDifferential ω z) z)
    (h : ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong ω γ g) : pathIntegral ω γ h = Φ (e Q) - Φ (e P) := by
  rw [(isPrimitiveAlong_of_chartAt_eq he hΦ).pathIntegral_eq h]
  simp only [Path.source, Path.target]

/-! ### Abel-Jacobi vectors and periods -/

/-- **Abel-Jacobi vector along a path.** For a family `b` of differentials with primitives along a
path `γ` from `P₀` to `P`, the vector of their line integrals along `γ`. Modulo the period
subgroup of `b` it depends only on `P₀` and `P`, and for a basis of the regular differentials of a
compact curve it lifts the Abel-Jacobi image of `P` with base place `P₀`. -/
def abelJacobiVec {n : ℕ} (b : Fin n → Ω[F⁄ℂ]) {P₀ P : Place ℂ F} (γ : Path P₀ P)
    (h : ∀ i, ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong (b i) γ g) : Fin n → ℂ :=
  fun i => pathIntegral (b i) γ (h i)

theorem abelJacobiVec_apply {n : ℕ} (b : Fin n → Ω[F⁄ℂ]) {P₀ P : Place ℂ F} (γ : Path P₀ P)
    (h : ∀ i, ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong (b i) γ g) (i : Fin n) :
    abelJacobiVec b γ h i = pathIntegral (b i) γ (h i) :=
  rfl

theorem abelJacobiVec_zero {n : ℕ} {P₀ P : Place ℂ F} (γ : Path P₀ P)
    (h : ∀ i, ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong ((0 : Fin n → Ω[F⁄ℂ]) i) γ g) :
    abelJacobiVec (0 : Fin n → Ω[F⁄ℂ]) γ h = 0 :=
  funext fun i => pathIntegral_zero γ (h i)

/-- **Period subgroup.** The subgroup of `ℂⁿ` generated by the Abel-Jacobi vectors of the family
`b` along the loops on which every member of `b` has a primitive. For a basis of the regular
differentials of a compact curve it is the period lattice. -/
def periodSubgroup {n : ℕ} (b : Fin n → Ω[F⁄ℂ]) : AddSubgroup (Fin n → ℂ) :=
  AddSubgroup.closure {u | ∃ (P : Place ℂ F) (γ : Path P P)
    (h : ∀ i, ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong (b i) γ g), u = abelJacobiVec b γ h}

theorem abelJacobiVec_mem_periodSubgroup {n : ℕ} (b : Fin n → Ω[F⁄ℂ]) {P : Place ℂ F}
    (γ : Path P P) (h : ∀ i, ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong (b i) γ g) :
    abelJacobiVec b γ h ∈ periodSubgroup b :=
  AddSubgroup.subset_closure ⟨P, γ, h, rfl⟩

/-- **Abel-Jacobi vectors modulo periods.** Modulo the period subgroup, the Abel-Jacobi vector
along a path depends only on the endpoints of the path. -/
theorem abelJacobiVec_sub_mem_periodSubgroup {n : ℕ} (b : Fin n → Ω[F⁄ℂ]) {P₀ P : Place ℂ F}
    (γ γ' : Path P₀ P) (h : ∀ i, ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong (b i) γ g)
    (h' : ∀ i, ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong (b i) γ' g) :
    abelJacobiVec b γ h - abelJacobiVec b γ' h' ∈ periodSubgroup b := by
  have hs : ∀ i, ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong (b i) γ'.symm g := fun i =>
    exists_isPrimitiveAlong_symm (h' i)
  have hL : ∀ i, ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong (b i) (γ.trans γ'.symm) g := fun i =>
    exists_isPrimitiveAlong_trans (h i) (hs i)
  convert abelJacobiVec_mem_periodSubgroup b (γ.trans γ'.symm) hL using 1
  funext i
  rw [Pi.sub_apply, abelJacobiVec_apply, abelJacobiVec_apply, abelJacobiVec_apply,
    pathIntegral_trans (h i) (hs i), pathIntegral_symm (h' i), sub_eq_add_neg]

/-- **Abel-Jacobi map on divisors.** For a choice of a path `γ P` from the base place `P₀` to each
place `P` along which every member of `b` has a primitive, the divisor `∑ m_P • P` goes to
`∑ m_P • abelJacobiVec b (γ P)`. Modulo the period subgroup of `b` it does not depend on the
paths. -/
def abelJacobiDiv {n : ℕ} (b : Fin n → Ω[F⁄ℂ]) {P₀ : Place ℂ F} (γ : ∀ P, Path P₀ P)
    (h : ∀ P i, ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong (b i) (γ P) g) : Divisor ℂ F →+ (Fin n → ℂ) :=
  Finsupp.liftAddHom fun P => zmultiplesHom (Fin n → ℂ) (abelJacobiVec b (γ P) (h P))

@[simp]
theorem abelJacobiDiv_single {n : ℕ} (b : Fin n → Ω[F⁄ℂ]) {P₀ : Place ℂ F} (γ : ∀ P, Path P₀ P)
    (h : ∀ P i, ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong (b i) (γ P) g) (P : Place ℂ F) (m : ℤ) :
    abelJacobiDiv b γ h (Finsupp.single P m) = m • abelJacobiVec b (γ P) (h P) := by
  simp [abelJacobiDiv]

theorem abelJacobiDiv_apply {n : ℕ} (b : Fin n → Ω[F⁄ℂ]) {P₀ : Place ℂ F} (γ : ∀ P, Path P₀ P)
    (h : ∀ P i, ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong (b i) (γ P) g) (D : Divisor ℂ F) :
    abelJacobiDiv b γ h D = D.sum fun P m => m • abelJacobiVec b (γ P) (h P) := by
  simp only [abelJacobiDiv, Finsupp.liftAddHom_apply]
  rfl

/-- **Abel-Jacobi map modulo periods.** Modulo the period subgroup, the Abel-Jacobi map on
divisors does not depend on the chosen paths. -/
theorem abelJacobiDiv_sub_mem_periodSubgroup {n : ℕ} (b : Fin n → Ω[F⁄ℂ]) {P₀ : Place ℂ F}
    (γ γ' : ∀ P, Path P₀ P) (h : ∀ P i, ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong (b i) (γ P) g)
    (h' : ∀ P i, ∃ g, IsPrimitiveAlong (b i) (γ' P) g) (D : Divisor ℂ F) :
    abelJacobiDiv b γ h D - abelJacobiDiv b γ' h' D ∈ periodSubgroup b := by
  induction D using Finsupp.induction_linear with
  | zero => simp
  | add D₁ D₂ h₁ h₂ =>
    rw [map_add, map_add, add_sub_add_comm]
    exact add_mem h₁ h₂
  | single P m =>
    rw [abelJacobiDiv_single, abelJacobiDiv_single, ← zsmul_sub]
    exact zsmul_mem (abelJacobiVec_sub_mem_periodSubgroup b (γ P) (γ' P) (h P) (h' P)) m

end Integral

end AlgebraicCurve
